preConditionHook:
// THE FAILURE TEST'S STALL WARNING. The position has been open stallBars bars,
// is still short of its first target, AND price has gone nowhere since -- the
// stallBars-bar high-low range is a small fraction of the initial risk (Grimes
// G06-11).
//
// THE CONJUNCTION IS ONE RULE BECAUSE EXITS ARE ORed: split across placements
// the three terms would each fire alone and take every trade off far too
// early. That is why NumBarsIfProfitable / NumBarsIfLosing exist as rules at
// all rather than as NumBars plus a filter.
//
// NOT NumBarsIfLosing, nor NumBarsIfBelowProfitThreshold: the
// RANGE-CONTRACTION term is the content here. Not FlatTradeScratchExit either
// -- that reads the position's PEAK profit and no price window.
//
// THE ENGINE HAS NO INITIAL-RISK ACCESSOR, so risk is a stopDistance INPUT IN
// PRICE POINTS (merge decision 24, the RewardRiskDeteriorationExit spelling).
//
// UNITS RECONCILED: ctx.OpenPositionProfit() is account CURRENCY while
// stopDistance is PRICE POINTS, so the profit term carries BigPointValue and
// the range term does not. BigPointValue is NOT currency converted while the
// profit accessors are -- TradeStation's own inconsistency, preserved as
// AtrProfitTarget and StopAtSignalBarRangeMultiple preserve it.
//
// The window mirrors EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest() call:
// seeded at bar 0, scanning bars 1..stallBars-1, STRICT comparison so a tie
// keeps the earliest bar. Extremes is EL SOURCE, so its comparisons carry the
// relational tolerance -- el_gt/el_lt, as in Breakout.
//
// SIDES ARE `same`. No MarketPosition guard, matching the NumBarsIf* family;
// the grid must keep stallBars >= 1, since BarsSinceEntry() is 0 while flat.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: stallBars - 1.
stallHigh = high[0];
stallLow = low[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)stallBars; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], stallHigh)) stallHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], stallLow)) stallLow = low[i];
}
